{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "15", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "08", "M": "13", "S": "28"}}, "news": [{"title": "Patna civic body approves four proposals; leasehold properties in six areas may go freehold", "para": "The Patna Municipal Corporation council has made significant strides by approving the conversion of leasehold properties to freehold. Additionally, plans for high-mast lights installation at thirty-five city locations will enhance safety. To boost water supply, five high-yield tube wells are set for construction. The council also scrutinized sanitation arrangements, penalizing outsourcing agencies, and deliberated on ward-specific civic matters for prompt action.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/patna-civic-body-approves-four-proposals-leasehold-properties-in-six-areas-may-go-freehold/133255484?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-51764/133255484.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Punjab begins mapping legitimate raw material supply for stone crushers", "para": "The Punjab Pollution Control Board is currently evaluating legitimate sources of raw materials for stone crushers. This scrutiny is designed to guarantee adherence to state regulations and policies. In the Ropar district, a significant number of stone crushers obtain materials from Punjab, Haryana, and Himachal Pradesh. Alarmingly, over 42% of these units have been found to violate pollution control laws.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/allied-industries/punjab-begins-mapping-legitimate-raw-material-supply-for-stone-crushers/133255470?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-280776/133255470.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "allied-industries"}, {"title": "After Mumbai, Pune set for plot-wise ready reckoner rates under micro-zoning", "para": "Pune and Mumbai are set to implement a detailed property valuation system that will transition from broad zoning classifications to more specific rates tied to individual plots and buildings. The state registration department is gearing up to adjust property rates for the upcoming year while introducing reforms like new stamp duty offices and mandatory land measurement. Additionally, linking Aadhaar may be required for all document registrations.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/after-mumbai-pune-set-for-plot-wise-ready-reckoner-rates-under-micro-zoning/133254987?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-76444/133254987.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}